# Readable text contrast

Never put important copy in a color that looks dark or washed out on the current background—especially dark mode.

## Use these tokens

- **`text-ink`**: headings, body copy, prices, credit counts, instructions, primary labels, success/status messages users must read
- **`text-stone`**: only secondary chrome (timestamps, “Your balance” captions, placeholders, inactive tabs)
- **`text-paper` on `bg-ink`**: primary buttons only

## Do not

- Style instructional or pack/body text with `text-stone`
- Use fixed dark Tailwind greens/reds like `text-emerald-700` / `text-red-700` for messages (nearly invisible on black). Prefer `text-ink` for success, `text-red-500` for errors
- Assume default inherited color is enough on tinted panels—set `text-ink` on important blocks

## Example

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — body and price muted; success invisible in dark mode
<p className="text-stone">{pack.body}</p>
<p className="text-emerald-700">{message}</p>

// ✅ GOOD
<p className="text-ink">{pack.body}</p>
<p className="font-semibold text-ink">{message}</p>
```
